        min_points=2,
        model_answer="The cork, like the water particles, only oscillates up and down about a fixed position; it is not carried along. The ripples therefore transfer energy (they make the cork move) but not matter.",
        hints=["What does the cork do, and what does it NOT do?",
               "Something reaches the cork and makes it move, but the water is not flowing past.",
               "Explain the cork's motion and what the wave does and does not transfer."],
