written("w10_frequency_up_wavelength", 10, 3, "10d",
        stem="A wave travels along a rope at a constant speed. Explain what happens to the wavelength if the frequency of the wave is doubled.",
        points=[P("speed = frequency × wavelength and the speed is fixed", ["v = f", "speed = frequency", "frequency times wavelength", "frequency × wavelength", "speed is constant", "speed stays the same", "same speed", "constant speed", "v is fixed"]),
                P("so the wavelength halves", ["halves", "halved", "half", "divided by two", "decreases to half"])],
        pitfalls=[PF(["wavelength doubles", "wavelength increases"], "At constant speed, v = f λ means a HIGHER frequency gives a SHORTER wavelength.")],
        model_answer="Wave speed = frequency × wavelength. The speed is fixed by the rope, so if the frequency is doubled the wavelength must halve to keep the product the same.",
        hints=["Which equation links speed, frequency and wavelength? Which of the three is fixed here?",
               "If the product f × λ must stay the same and f doubles, what must λ do?",
               "State the equation, say which quantity is constant, and state the change in wavelength."],
        keywords="v = f λ, speed constant, wavelength halves",
        sample_pass=["Since v = fλ and the speed is constant, doubling the frequency halves the wavelength", "speed stays the same so the wavelength must be half as long"],
        sample_fail=["The wavelength doubles too", "The wave speeds up"])

